<title>USA: Dunavant sees 97/98 US cotton acreage at 13.8 mln.</title>
<headline>Dunavant sees 97/98 US cotton acreage at 13.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cotton merchant William B. Duvavant Jr. pegged U.S. 1997/98 planted cotton acreage at 13.8 million acres compared with 14.2 million acres in 1996/97.</p>
<p>Dunavant said acreage, with a 650-lb yield and a five abandonment will produce a crop of 17.75 million to 17.85 million bales.</p>
<p>Exports of U.S. cotton were seen at 6.9 million bales and import as negligible, he said.</p>
<p>Carryover will fall to between 4.3 million and 4.4 million bales from a projection of 4.5 million to 4.6 million bales for this crop season.</p>
</text>
